 "code_fixes_required_before_running": [
  "score_cid.py: --gate-assessor. Today args.assessor is passed to BOTH classify_essay and gate_verdict (score_cid.py lines 72-77), so scoring the gpt-5.4-mini arms with gpt-4o moves the gate and the stance classifier at once. Evidence it matters: on the one already-scored gated cell c04310fab9, one of the two label disagreements is a GATE disagreement (q2 DISCLAIMED under gpt-4o-mini vs REFUSED under gpt-4o), not a classifier disagreement.",
  "score_cid.py: --run-tag, mirroring political_questions.py. Without it a second assessor draw on the same cid reads draw 1's cache and Arm A cannot separate assessor identity from assessor nondeterminism (sd 0.252, section 36).",
  "compare_assessors.py: load() builds cache_<cid>_<assessor>.json with no prompt/gate suffix (line 27), so it cannot open a _gate3 or _explicit cache. Needs --tag before any gpt-5.4-mini cell can be compared per statement."
 ],
 "wall_clock": "measured 1.17 s per gpt-4o assessor call sequentially (20 calls in 23.4 s). The full design is 4*3*62*2 + 72*62 = 5952 calls ~= 116 min sequential, ~40 min at three concurrent processes. A fully cached re-read of a 62-statement cell is 0.56 s and costs nothing."
